# Copy to `.dev.vars` (git-ignored) for `wrangler dev`.
#
# These are PLACEHOLDERS and should stay that way. Every feature they gate is
# simply off when unconfigured, which is the intended local behaviour:
#   - push degrades to a logged no-op
#   - DELETE /me returns a clean failure instead of calling Identity Toolkit
# Do not put real service-account credentials here to "make push work" locally.
#
# Auth still works without a Firebase project: `@eigeninteractive/server/testing` mints
# local tokens the real auth middleware accepts, which is how the test suites
# exercise the real DO and real D1 with no cloud account.

FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=placeholder
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=placeholder@placeholder.iam.gserviceaccount.com
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY="placeholder"
BOT_SIGNING_SECRET=dev-only-secret
